1. The problem requires us to find a root for the tree such that no subtree (except the whole tree) contains vertices of different colors.
2. We first build the graph from the input edges.
3. We identify any edge where the two connected nodes have different colors. These are potential candidates for further checking.
4. If there are no such edges, all nodes have the same color and any node can be chosen as root; we return "YES" with any node.
5. Otherwise, we perform DFS starting from each endpoint of the first differing edge to check if it is possible to choose one of them as the root such that all subtrees rooted at their children have consistent colors.
6. If neither works, we print "NO".

